# The Big Picture

System design is fundamentally about answering:

> **How do we build a system that remains correct, fast, reliable, secure and maintainable as users, data and traffic grow?**

A simple application might look like:

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    U[User] --> C[Client]
    C --> S[Server]
    S --> DB[(Database)]
```

A production system becomes:

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    U[User] --> DNS[DNS]
    DNS --> CDN[CDN]
    CDN --> RP[Reverse Proxy]
    RP --> LB[Load Balancer]

    LB --> API1[API Server]
    LB --> API2[API Server]
    LB --> API3[API Server]

    API1 --> CACHE[(Redis Cache)]
    API2 --> CACHE
    API3 --> CACHE

    API1 --> DB[(Primary DB)]
    API2 --> DB
    API3 --> DB

    DB --> R1[(Read Replica)]
    DB --> R2[(Read Replica)]

    API1 --> Q[Message Queue]
    Q --> W[Workers]

    W --> OBJ[(Object Storage)]
```

The key lesson:

> **Don't start with technologies. Start with requirements, traffic, data, failure modes and constraints.**

