# 2. IP Addresses

Machines communicate over networks using IP addresses.

Example:

```text
203.0.113.10
```

IPv4:

```text
192.168.1.10
```

IPv6:

```text
2001:db8::1
```

The important system-design principle:

> Clients need a network address to communicate with a service.

Modern systems generally hide infrastructure IPs behind:

* DNS
* Load balancers
* Reverse proxies
* CDNs
* API gateways
* Service meshes

