# 9. REST

REST treats data as resources.

Example:

```http
GET    /users
GET    /users/123
POST   /users
PUT    /users/123
DELETE /users/123
```

Characteristics:

* Resource-oriented
* HTTP-based
* Stateless
* Cache-friendly
* Simple to understand

### Strengths

* Easy to debug
* Widely supported
* Good tooling
* Easy browser integration
* Good for public APIs

### Weaknesses

* Over-fetching
* Under-fetching
* Multiple requests
* Versioning challenges

