# 13. Horizontal Scaling

Scaling out means adding more machines.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    LB[Load Balancer]

    LB --> S1[Server]
    LB --> S2[Server]
    LB --> S3[Server]
    LB --> S4[Server]
```

Advantages:

* More capacity
* Better availability
* Fault tolerance
* Elasticity

But horizontal scaling requires:

* Stateless services
* Shared/session storage strategy
* Load balancing
* Distributed locking where necessary
* Data scaling

