# 15. Database Indexing

An index allows a database to find data without scanning every row.

Without index:

```text
Row 1
Row 2
Row 3
...
Row 1,000,000
```

With index:

```text
user_id → row location
```

Example:

```sql
CREATE INDEX idx_users_email
ON users(email);
```

### Trade-off

Indexes:

```text
READ PERFORMANCE ↑
WRITE COST ↑
STORAGE ↑
```

Don't index everything.

Index according to actual query patterns.

