# 21. CAP Theorem

CAP concerns distributed systems.

The three properties are:

```text
C = Consistency
A = Availability
P = Partition Tolerance
```

The core idea:

> When a network partition occurs, a distributed system has to make a trade-off between consistency and availability.

```mermaid
graph TD
    C[Consistency]
    A[Availability]
    P[Partition Tolerance]

    C --- A
    A --- P
    P --- C
```

In real distributed systems, partition tolerance is generally unavoidable.

Therefore the practical question becomes:

```text
During a network partition:

Prefer consistency?
OR
Prefer availability?
```

