# 28. Rate Limiting

Rate limiting protects systems from excessive traffic.

Example:

```text
100 requests / minute / user
```

Algorithms:

### Fixed Window

```text
00:00 → 00:59
100 requests
```

### Sliding Window

Continuously evaluates the recent period.

### Token Bucket

Tokens accumulate over time.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    R[Requests] --> RL[Rate Limiter]

    RL -->|Allowed| API[API]
    RL -->|Rejected| X[429 Too Many Requests]
```

Rate limiting protects against:

* Abuse
* Bots
* Accidental overload
* DDoS-like application traffic
* Expensive API usage

