# 30. Idempotency

An operation is idempotent when repeating it produces the same intended result.

This matters enormously in distributed systems.

Example:

```text
POST /payments
Idempotency-Key: abc123
```

First request:

```text
abc123 → payment created
```

Retry:

```text
abc123 → return existing payment
```

Instead of:

```text
Payment 1
Payment 2
Payment 3
```

### Critical for

* Payments
* Orders
* Webhooks
* Job submission
* File processing
* Distributed retries

